<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB confirms Sri Lanka wheat sale, Egypt unclear.</title>
<headline>AWB confirms Sri Lanka wheat sale, Egypt unclear.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) confirmed on Monday that it had sold 50,000 tonnes of hard wheat to Sri Lanka at US$191.95 a tonne cost and freight for June shipment.</p>
<p>It was commenting on a Reuters report from Chicago on the sale.</p>
<p>The AWB also said it had no immediate comment on a Cairo report that Egypt was seeking 50,000 tonnes of American, Australian or French wheat.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
